# What `git archive` -- and so the GitHub release zipball, which Zenodo
# archives -- leaves out: the lab (lab/, the dnsjax-lab package of flows
# and features in development, not shipped with release archives
# outside GitHub), every file written for coding agents (the CLAUDE.md
# notes, .claude/), the development configuration (CI, git and hook
# settings, uv's pinned interpreter and lock file), and the contributor
# guide, which describes this repository rather than the solver.  The
# PyPI sdist holds the same files (pyproject.toml's source-include).
# The with-lab asset a GitHub release attaches leaves out the agent
# files alone, as lab/scripts/release/prepare_release.py's agent_file
# names them: change the two together.
/lab export-ignore
/CONTRIBUTING.md export-ignore
/uv.lock export-ignore
/.claude export-ignore
CLAUDE.md export-ignore
/.github export-ignore
/.gitattributes export-ignore
/.gitignore export-ignore
/.python-version export-ignore
/prek.toml export-ignore
